Show the contents of a text file in the in-world filesystem.

usage: @fcat <path>

Prints the file at an absolute VFS path. It refuses a binary or ELF file
(use @ftype to check a file's kind, or @fget to download it), so a compiled
image cannot flood your connection. A very large text file is shown only up
to the first 64 KB, with a note.

Wizard only.

Example:
  @fcat /src/greet.kp
      Show the Kobold source.

See also @fls, @ftype, @fedit, @fget.
